Your own mod or integration remains your own work and may be distributed under
your own license. This section does not grant rights to RS Integration beyond
those expressly stated in Section 2.2.

### 2.4 Termination

This permission terminates automatically if you materially violate this
license and do not cure the violation within 30 days after receiving written
notice. After termination, you must stop using and distributing the Licensed
API. End users may continue using already obtained official RS Integration
releases under Section 1.

### 2.5 API Compatibility

The version and compatibility rules published in the RSI API documentation
describe the current compatibility policy. They are not a warranty of
indefinite support, a promise to backport fixes, or an obligation to maintain
every prior API version.

RSI may introduce incompatible API changes in a new major version as described
by that policy. Consumers of the Licensed API are responsible for checking the
available API version at runtime and adapting their integrations when they
choose to upgrade RS Integration. Nothing in this section revokes rights
already granted for an official release that a consumer continues to use.

